Single-page marketing site (German-language, industrial services business
"HIM" in Hamburg) built on Next.js App Router.

- **`app/`** — routes only. `app/page.tsx` composes the homepage purely from
  section components in order (Hero → Intro → Services → Trust → Gallery →
  Faq → Cta → Contact → ImageBanner). `app/layout.tsx` wraps every route with
  `Header`/`Footer`. Legal pages (`impressum`, `datenschutz`) are separate
  routes.
- **`components/sections/`** — one component per homepage section, matched
  1:1 to a data object in `data/site.ts`. To change homepage copy, edit
  `data/site.ts`, not the section components — components are presentational
  and read from these exported objects.
- **`components/layout/`** — header, footer, and `image-banner`/`logo-mark`.
- **`components/ui/`** — shadcn/ui primitives (installed via
  `components.json`, style `radix-nova`, Radix + `lucide-react` icons).
  Regenerate/add primitives through the shadcn CLI conventions implied by
  `components.json` rather than hand-rolling equivalents. Notable custom
  primitive: `theme-image.tsx`, a wrapper around `next/image` for the
  Unsplash-backed imagery pattern below.
- **`data/site.ts`** — all copy/content for the homepage sections as typed
  exported consts (`hero`, `intro`, `services`, `trustSection`,
  `gallerySection`, `faqs`, `contactSection`, etc.), including nav items and
  footer links.
- **`data/images.ts`** — image content is Unsplash-hosted, not local: each
  `SiteImage` is `{ id, alt, credit }`, and `unsplashUrl(id, width)` builds
  the URL. `next.config.ts` whitelists `images.unsplash.com` via
  `images.remotePatterns` — any new external image host must be added there.
- **`lib/utils.ts`** — `cn()` (clsx + tailwind-merge), the standard shadcn
  helper.

## Styling

Tailwind v4, CSS-first config in `app/globals.css` (no `tailwind.config.*`).

- Theme tokens (`--background`, `--primary`, `--secondary`, `--accent`, etc.)
  are defined as a "warm concrete + harbor teal + safety orange" palette in
  `:root`/`.dark`, then re-exposed via `@theme inline` for Tailwind utility
  generation. Prefer the semantic tokens (`bg-primary`,
  `text-muted-foreground`, ...) over raw palette colors.
- `--radius` is set to `2px` sitewide (deliberately sharp/industrial
  corners) — don't reintroduce rounded defaults.
- Reusable utility classes are defined in `@layer utilities` in
  `globals.css`: `.container-page`, `.section-padding`,
  `.surface-soft`/`.surface-elevated`, `.section-divider`,
  `.brand-gradient`, `.accent-gradient`, `.hero-grid`. Use these instead of
  re-implementing the same patterns inline.
- Legacy `blue-*` Tailwind utilities are remapped to the harbor teal palette
  for compatibility — new code should use `harbor-*`/semantic tokens
  directly rather than `blue-*`.

## Imports

ESLint enforces `simple-import-sort` (imports and exports) — import order is
auto-fixable via `pnpm lint --fix`, don't hand-sort.

## Boundaries

- Never commit without explicit review.
- Never modify `.env*` or lockfiles without asking first.
- Don't add a test framework or test commands — none exist yet; ask before introducing one.
- Don't add new dependencies without checking they're actually needed and not already covered by an existing shadcn/Radix primitive.